WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:03.458
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:08.240
NARRATOR: As the music
industry went digital,

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:11.390
the turntable seemed
destined for the scrap heap.

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:13.550
But this analog
technology defied

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:15.470
predictions and survived.

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:18.080
With a sound that's
arguably fuller and more

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.360
natural than compressed
digital formats,

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:23.540
this retro technology
is attracting new fans.

00:00:24.894 --> 00:00:27.710
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:32.200
In an age when media players
are digitized and pocket-sized,

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.880
the turntable plays on.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.030
The use of high tech
composites like carbon fiber

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:41.730
puts a modern spin
on this technology

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:44.595
bringing the record player
into the 21st century.

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:51.700
Production starts with a
thick square of cast acrylic.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:54.160
The technician drills
a hole in the center.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:57.370
It will be a reference point
as he transforms this square

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:58.660
into the turntable platter.

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.190
A computerized tool cuts a
circle shape out of the square.

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:11.350
The disk then spins while
another computer guided tool

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:13.330
enlarges the center
hole to size it

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:14.590
for the platters main bearing.

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:19.300
The next whole precisely
cuts the surface of the disk

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:20.650
to give it the correct angle.

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:29.580
Computerized tools transform
this small aluminum disk

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:32.070
into the counterweights
main component.

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:35.580
The counterweight balances the
tone arm to keep the stylus

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:37.740
in the groove of an LP.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.860
They slope the surface and
cut holes for attachments

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:42.255
and for installing the part.

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:46.935
Finally, they cut a
triangle out of the circle.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:55.280
This takes the part to its
final shape and weight,

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:58.850
from a flat disk to a precisely
crafted counterweight.

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:05.630
Next, the platform for
the tone arm takes shape.

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:08.660
It's designed to cradle all the
parts at the end of the tone

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:12.680
arm including a cylindrical
housing for a spring mechanism

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:14.900
and an egg-shaped housing
containing a bearing.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.680
A technician now
assembles the tone arm

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:22.770
beginning with a tapered
to made of carbon fiber.

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:25.770
It's a high tech composite
that's extremely stiff.

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:28.875
So there should be no structural
weakness in this crucial part.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:32.550
The technician threads
a pre-assembled wiring

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:34.410
loom through the arm to.

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:37.950
It's special wire for
high frequency transfer.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:40.170
These wires have been
encased in copper

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:43.050
to keep out ambient radiation
that would interfere

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.240
with the tone arms operation.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:49.140
The carbon fiber tube also
acts as a radiation shield.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:52.800
He mixes epoxy resin that he
then dabs around the inner rim

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:55.110
of the bearing housing,
which has by now

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:56.205
been equipped with the bearing.

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:03.420
He inserts the tone arm
tube into the housing.

00:03:08.110 --> 00:03:10.225
The tube adheres to
the glue-coated rim.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:14.290
But before a totally
bonds, the technician

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:17.080
scrutinizes the alignment.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:19.420
He makes adjustments if
needed, and then he'll

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:21.775
clamp the assembly to
allow the glue to cure.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.750
With a turntable
tone arm now upright,

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:30.570
he solders the wires that
are protruding from the joint

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:32.790
to external wiring
for the amplifier.

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:39.620
And once all the
connections have been made,

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.765
he inserts the wires
into the metal joint.

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:49.030
Ensconced in this joint, the
connections are well protected

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:50.305
and can't be pulled apart.

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:56.050
He equips the main
counterweight component with two

00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:57.580
thick steel beams for balance.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:01.600
He slides the counterweight
onto a third beam,

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:04.960
which has been installed
in the egg-shaped housing.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:06.895
This completes the
turntable tone arm.

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:19.029
Next, they encase the electric
motor and its metal housing

00:04:19.029 --> 00:04:21.310
and they build the record deck.

00:04:21.310 --> 00:04:24.250
They mount the motor to the
two-tiered deck designed

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:26.290
to absorb any vibration.

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:29.380
The aluminum
sub-chassis is next.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:31.930
They link it to the motor
with the drive belt.

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:35.140
Then they give the belt drive
system a test spin to confirm

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:36.085
that it runs smoothly.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.310
They now install
the acrylic platter,

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:41.675
felt mat, and tone arm.

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:45.320
With this turntable
now fully assembled,

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:48.110
it's time for the vinyl test.

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:51.080
The record spins and the
stylus traces the grooves.

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:58.990
The analog sound fills the
room proving this technology

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:02.010
stands the test of time.

